        <detaileddescription>
<para>── compact / flushOnce ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────</para>
<para>After this call every live mutation resides in a leaf node and all tombstones have been purged. This is the analogue of a full compaction in an LSM tree, but incurs significantly less I/O because each mutation has already been partially propagated.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>OkVoid() on success.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Return value.</para>
</simplesect>
Calls: lk(), flushAll(), OkVoid(). </para>
